Package: aobview
Title: View Spatial Data in Its Own Coordinate Reference System
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Michael", "Sumner", , "mdsumner@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: A convenience front end for 'allonboard' map scenes: 'view(x)'
    draws spatial objects in a self-contained HTML page, in their own
    coordinate reference system or a polar view chosen for them, through
    the lean core package 'aobcore'. Vector data are read through 'wk' (any
    geometry it can handle, or a data frame with such a column, 'sf'
    included), from Arrow streams and tables (a 'duckdb' result, a GDAL
    layer) and from 'gdalraster' feature sets, and reprojected with 'PROJ';
    a string is WKT text or the path, URL or data source name of a raster
    or vector source, read with 'gdalraster'. This is an early skeleton;
    the package name is a placeholder.
